Repair proposal for Item `host` — AC-1 `when` step "square six" (no concept reaches threshold 9).

The change is a new concept in the product document, owned by the Product Owner. No binding change is needed, so the System Architect is not involved. The Story stays unchanged.

## Decision behind the proposal

The step "square six" is a well-formed action for the `when` block, so no rewrite of the Item is needed. The only candidate, `halve` (score 2), cannot be widened: the product description states "The calculator offers separate Halve and Square controls. Halve divides the entered number by two; Square multiplies the entered number by itself." Square is therefore a different Public interface item, not a variation of the Halve control's use. Widening `halve` to admit squaring would merge two separate controls into one concept. A new `when` concept for the Square control is the correct repair.

## Exact change — `docs/product/product.yaml`

Add one entry to `concepts.when`, after the existing `halve` entry. No other concept, no `glossary` entry, and no `description` text is touched.

Before:

```json
    "when": [
      {
        "concept": "halve",
        "means": "Halve the entered number once.",
        "terms": []
      }
    ],
```

After:

```json
    "when": [
      {
        "concept": "halve",
        "means": "Halve the entered number once.",
        "terms": []
      },
      {
        "concept": "square",
        "means": "Square the entered number once, multiplying it by itself.",
        "terms": []
      }
    ],
```

